"{\n  \"entry_block_ref\": \"read_user_request\",\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"Skill metadata name: linear\",\n    \"Skill metadata description: Manage issues, projects & team workflows in Linear. Use when the user wants to read, create or updates tickets in Linear.\",\n    \"Skill metadata short-description: Manage Linear issues in Codex\",\n    \"Interface display_name: Linear\",\n    \"Interface short_description: Manage Linear issues in Codex\",\n    \"Interface icon_small: ./assets/linear-small.svg\",\n    \"Interface icon_large: ./assets/linear.png\",\n    \"Interface default_prompt: Use Linear context to triage or update relevant issues for this task, with clear next actions.\",\n    \"MCP dependency: linear (Linear MCP server), transport streamable_http, url https://mcp.linear.app/mcp.\",\n    \"Follow these steps in order. Do not skip steps.\",\n    \"Linear MCP server must be connected and accessible via OAuth.\",\n    \"Confirm access to the relevant Linear workspace, teams, and projects.\",\n    \"Step 0: Set up Linear MCP (if not already configured).\",\n    \"If any MCP call fails because Linear MCP is not connected, pause and set it up.\",\n    \"Step 1: Clarify the user's goal and scope (e.g., issue triage, sprint planning, documentation audit, workload balance). Confirm team/project, priority, labels, cycle, and due dates as needed.\",\n    \"Step 2: Select the appropriate workflow (see Practical Workflows below) and identify the Linear MCP tools you will need. Confirm required identifiers (issue ID, project ID, team key) before calling tools.\",\n    \"Step 3: Execute Linear MCP tool calls in logical batches: Read first (list/get/search) to build context. Create or update next (issues, projects, labels, comments) with all required fields. For bulk operations, explain grouping logic before applying changes.\",\n    \"Step 4: Summarize results, call out remaining gaps or blockers, and propose next actions (additional issues, label changes, assignments, or follow-up comments).\",\n    \"After successful login, the user will have to restart codex. You should finish your answer and tell them so when they try again they can continue with Step 1.\"\n  ],\n  \"declared_context_keys\": [\n    \"user_request\",\n    \"linear_mcp_configuration_status\"\n  ],\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"read_user_request\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Read the user's request\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": \"context\",\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"read_user_request_ir\",\n          \"opcode\": \"read_user_request\",\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"context_key\",\n              \"identifier\": \"user_request\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"outputs\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"result\",\n              \"identifier\": \"user_request_text\",\n              \"semantic_name\": \"user request text\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {\n            \"skill_name\": \"linear\",\n            \"skill_description\": \"Manage issues, projects & team workflows in Linear. Use when the user wants to read, create or updates tickets in Linear.\",\n            \"skill_short_description\": \"Manage Linear issues in Codex\",\n            \"default_prompt\": \"Use Linear context to triage or update relevant issues for this task, with clear next actions.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"instruction_ref\": \"dispatch_to_check_mcp\",\n          \"opcode\": \"dispatch\",\n          \"inputs\": [],\n          \"outputs\": [],\n          \"constraints\": [],\n          \"metadata\": {}\n        }\n      ],\n      \"constraints\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"block_ref\": \"check_mcp_configuration\",\n      \"block_name\": \"Check whether Linear MCP is already configured\",\n      \"data_source_kind\": \"context\",\n      \"instructions\": [\n        {\n          \"instruction_